  "details": "I would like a reservation feature for instances that allows users to join a waiting line starting about 10 minutes before the event. At the scheduled time, invitations would be sent out by lottery to users in the waiting line.\n\nLet me explain the background of this request.\n\nCurrently, in Japan, volunteer-led VRC events are thriving and have become incredibly popular. There are two main methods for gathering participants for these events:\n\n１：First-come, first-served method: Participation queues are sent simultaneously to the instance leader.\n\n２：Lottery-based method: Participants send invitation requests to the instance leader, who then randomly selects attendees.\n\nEach method has its advantages and disadvantages. However, the lottery-based method has recently become the standard, placing a significant burden on the organizers. To resolve this issue, I would like to propose a feature in VRChat that can process invitation requests randomly on behalf of the organizers.",
